  "body": "Two P0 gaps in the fixture box laws: silent crashes the post gate let through. Both were found surveying #339.\n\n## What changed\nNew `crates/sim/src/verify/stack_span.rs` gives both laws one rule for the z span of the tool stack along a move.\n- Each piece of the tip path (the straight move, or one of an arc's 3-D chords) spans `[min(floor, piece low), piece high]`.\n- A band `above..above+len` is judged over `[z_lo+above, z_hi+above+len]` with the existing strict `band_hits_box`.\n- That window only ever grows compared with the old one. On a level move it is the old window, with the same arithmetic.\n\n**#425, law c2 (`bands_vs_fixtures_held`).** Every band, including the flute column and the leaning enclosure, is judged over its true span along the move, floored at the move's deepest end. Before, every band was pinned at `min(from.z, to.z)`.\n- The repro: a ramp z0→40 under a clamp arm at z100..120 over its high end, holder top at 130 there. It now reports `FixtureHit(Holder)`.\n- A non-finite z now counts as a hit. The old `min` dropped NaN silently.\n\n**#424, law d2 (`rapids_vs_fixtures_held`, upright branch).** After the flute disc (unchanged, still reported as `Rapid`), the rapid now checks every band above the flute over the rapid's span, each named when struck: shank, **the `HolderStack`'s own bands**, and the spindle housing at `holder.top`. The flute column above the tip comes last.\n- The vertical retract beside the r20-holder bolt reports Holder. A low traverse past a tall bolt reports Shank, or Spindle.\n- **Strict-dip silences kept:** a retract off a mounting face, a plunge onto a face, a traverse riding a face, and flush contact all stay silent. Penetrating by 0.001 reports.\n\n**With #381 (merged).** The upright-rapid stack is built from the same `HolderStack` the bands law and the posed sweep take, so a modelled holder body is judged band by band. `fixture_stack_span::an_upright_rapid_reads_a_modelled_holder_bodys_bands` pins it: a slim r5 cylinder clears the bolt, and the body's r20 collar must hit.\n\n`docs/decisions/424-425-fixture-law-gaps.md`\n\n## How tested\n- **New sim `fixture_stack_span`** (8 tests):\n  - the #424 retract, also through `rapids_vs_workholding` for turning, fixed and rotary steel;\n  - the traverse naming Shank and Spindle;\n  - an overhanging arm caught by the flute column;\n  - the strict-dip pins;\n  - the #425 ramp in both directions, and a helical ramp;\n  - level moves unchanged;\n  - the HolderStack test.\n\n  6 of the 8 fail on main before this fix. The strict-dip and level-move pins pass on both, by design.\n- **New app `fixture_law_gaps`** (3 tests): a face program whose retract, and whose plunge start, carry the holder into a clamp arm. `posting::verification_gate` refuses with \"Face1: holder at move N strikes a fixture\", and generation warns `FixtureHit`. The same arms at the holder's top post clean. The two blocking tests fail on main.\n- **Existing suites, no verdict changed:** fixtures, rotary_fixtures, tool_body, posting, and the posed/rapids suites pass. The window is a superset of the old one, so old hits are never dropped; new hits come only from steel the stack really reaches. On long ramps the enclosing window can over-report a graze. That trade-off is chosen over an exact sheared sweep, which would drop some existing verdicts; see the decisions file.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --tests -D warnings` is clean. `scripts/gate.sh quick` passes except #415, which is red on main.\n\n## Merging with #430 (fixture mesh)\nA trial merge is clean. #430 wraps these laws and can only clear a hit. On a meshed fixture, an upright-rapid holder hit reads as `Rapid` rather than `Holder`. That's a label difference only; the post is blocked either way.\n\nChangelog: Fixture collisions: an upright rapid now checks the whole tool stack (shank, holder, spindle housing) and a ramp checks each band over its true height span, closing two missed-collision gaps (#424, #425)\n\nFixes #424\nFixes #425\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
